.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-TUI 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-tui \- a full-screen menu to run, trace, draw or export
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar tui\fR [\-\-theme <name>] [<folder>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A full-screen menu in the terminal. Pick a .kstar file in <folder> (the
current one by default, three folders deep), then run the whole file, or
pick a machine in it and trace it on a word step by step (Left and Right
step through the run), draw it, draw a run of it, or export it as Rust,
Python or JSON. Esc goes back, q leaves.
.PP
To list a file's machines it runs the file quietly, as \fBkstar trace\fR
does. Everything here is also a command: \fBkstar run\fR, \fBkstar trace\fR,
\fBdraw\fR in a program, and \fBkstar export\fR. It needs a terminal; it does not
start when output is redirected, or with NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<name>\fR
the colours of the screen: auto (the default: the terminal's own colours), light, dark or high-contrast. KSTAR_THEME and the config file work as for \fBkstar run\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar tui\fR
pick a program in this folder
.TP
\fBkstar tui examples\fR
pick one of the examples
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
